# Original owner sandbox observer controls

This local component suite checks a private read-only consuming composition.
The constructor accepts only the existing InstalledEntryUnit; it derives policy,
manager, unit, deadlines, image and stream expectations from that same owner.
It queries the original manager connection and observes the manager-selected PID.
The resulting object offers revalidation, not start, release or completion.

Run `python -B tools/bootstrap-sandbox-owner-074/check.py host`, then `194`, `188`
and `metadata`. Host and metadata share the Windows Cargo cache and must not run
concurrently. GNU and MSRV caches are independent. Output lanes are exclusive;
historical baseline reexecution refuses. `-final` lanes retain corrected component
checks separately, never retry an original live experiment.

The fixed commands run models, reply/value parsing, an owned ordinary helper
refusal and preceding selected controls. They do not run the consuming production
constructor on a real managed sandbox, create a service or cgroup, change clocks,
install, send original messages or run a workload. The existing child modes still
refuse authority. Positive manager/sandbox integration, full loaded-unit settings,
the child enrollment exchange and original-delivery provenance remain required.
An observed pre-existing matching unit is not evidence this owner launched it.

After reviewing and committing exact sources, run
`python -B tools/bootstrap-sandbox-owner-074/retain.py --checked-commit SHA`.
The retainer checks exact source snapshots, commands, test counts, raw logs,
qualification digest and committed sources; it refuses incomplete/failed lanes
and packet overwrite. Initial development outcomes are explicitly labelled
tool-output summaries; they are not reconstructed raw receipts.
